## Modeling a Library Book

A book has a title, author, and a checkout status. With methods, you can change its state just like a real library.

### The Book Struct

```xiom
type Book = {
  title: Str;
  author: Str;
  checked_out: Bool;
}
```

### Checking Out a Book

Methods on structs can mutate fields. Here `checkout` sets `checked_out` to `true`:

```xiom
fn Book.checkout(self) {
  checked_out = true;
}
```

Note: inside a method, `self` is implicit — you access fields directly, no `self.` prefix.

### Checking Availability

```xiom
fn Book.is_available(self) -> Bool {
  return !checked_out;
}
```

### Using the Library

```xiom
var book = Book{
  title: "The Hobbit";
  author: "J.R.R. Tolkien";
  checked_out: false;
};

book.is_available();  // true
book.checkout();
book.is_available();  // false
```

### Returning a Book

Add a `return_book` method that sets `checked_out` back to `false`:

```xiom
fn Book.return_book(self) {
  checked_out = false;
}
```

